--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/4-5, [temp.inst]/2: deducing os<wchar_t, T> from an
os<char, tr<char>> fails at wchar_t vs char, and nothing requires
os<wchar_t, tr<char>> to be complete.  The front end instantiates the
pattern with the deduced T = tr<char> anyway; sb<wchar_t, tr<char>>::put is
ill-formed and dropped ("C++ front-end dropped the body of function
'put'").  The verdict is right here, but the bogus instance is a hard error
risk; in libc++ <sstream> it drops basic_streambuf<wchar_t,
char_traits<char>>::xsputn / xsgetn (streambuf:268/276;
cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_sstream_insert.desc).  Pre-existing (bin53).
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
